course: dictionary
lesson: 9655
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Mia's science project is due on Friday, and her submission must be uploaded by 5 pm.» A due date and uploading tell you that submission here means the work she hands in.
explain: «The army was beaten into submission.» Beaten is the clue. Submission here means giving in to someone more powerful, and it is a different meaning from the homework one. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. «Islam is a faith in one God, and the word Islam means "submission", giving your life to God.» The sentence explains the meaning for you, so you can see that here submission means giving yourself humbly to God.
fact: A submission is something you hand in to be judged or checked, like homework, a competition entry or a form.
fact: Submission is also the act of handing something in, or giving in to someone more powerful, as in «beaten into submission».
fact: In law, a submission is an argument or statement given to a judge or committee.
fact: «Islam» means «submission», giving your life to God.
fact: Useful phrases: «submission date», «deadline for submissions», «in submission», «into submission».
exercise: «Entries for the art contest close on Monday; the final submission date is 4 pm.» What does submission mean here? | *Something you hand in to be judged | A bird that lives near the sea | Giving in to a stronger team | A sad, grey song
exercise: «The soldiers were beaten into submission.» What does submission mean? | Running very fast to escape | Singing loudly to a crowd | *Giving in to someone more powerful
exercise: «Islam» means «submission», giving your life to God. Which phrase matches this meaning? | *Giving your life to God | Writing a long essay | Sharing your lunch with friends | A deadline for homework
test: «Ella's maths submission was late because the online submit button wouldn't work.» What is a submission here? | A type of cloud | A kind of storm at sea | *Homework handed in, like a piece of work | A long walk to school
test: In a court of law, what is a submission? | A school uniform | A type of holiday | A bowl of soup | *An argument or statement given to a judge
exam: Which phrase means the day by which work must be handed in? | Sleeping bag | *Submission date | Sunny afternoon | Bread and butter
